{
  "requirement": "The `habeas` CLI MUST use `clap` to define and parse its commands and options.",
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "**Verdict:** `requirements.cli.clap` is satisfied. The requirement says the CLI must use `clap` to define and parse its commands and options.\n\n**Implementation**\n- `Cargo.toml:55` depends on `clap` 4.6.7 with the `derive` feature.\n- `src/main.rs` defines the whole CLI with clap derives:\n  - `Cli` uses `#[derive(Parser)]`.\n  - `Command`, `MdbookCommand` and `HookCommand` use `#[derive(Subcommand)]`.\n  - Options, arguments, aliases, hidden commands and `ArgGroup` constraints are all clap attributes.\n- `fn main` parses with `Cli::parse()` (line 101), and every later branch dispatches on the clap-produced values.\n- Each of these items carries `{impl}` for `requirements.cli.clap`.\n- A search of `src` found no hand-rolled argument parsing, such as `env::args`.\n- The per-command behaviours in `Command` and `main` are marked as implementing their own requirements: `cli.status`, `cli.add_input*`, `authoring.*`, `cli.invocation`, `cli.setup` and `cli.mdbook`. The workspace-config load block is marked with the `configuration.*` requirements. They are not unmarked extra behaviour.\n\n**Tests**\n- `tests/cli.rs::clap_defines_commands_options_and_usage_errors` checks:\n  - `--help` output starts with `Usage: habeas <COMMAND>`.\n  - Every public command appears in the help.\n  - The hidden `hook` command does not appear in the help.\n  - `status --help` lists `--all` and `--verbose`.\n  - The `author-evidence` alias resolves to `author`.\n  - Three usage-error cases (an unknown option, a missing required argument, and conflicting `author` arguments) exit with code 2 and print a usage message.\n- `tests/commands.rs::add_input_requires_one_target_and_mode_and_resets_changed_records` is also marked `{test}` for this requirement. It checks that clap's `ArgGroup` rules reject missing, duplicate or conflicting targets and modes. These failures exit with code 2 and print `Usage: habeas add-input`.\n- Together the tests cover clap's definition of commands and options, its parsing, and its error handling.\n\nNo gaps found.",
